Figure \ref{figTree3D} shows an  example of a $3$-metric dimensional tree.   In this case $\mathcal{M}(T)=\{w,w'\}$, $\ter(w)=\ter(w')=2$ and $\varsigma(w)=\varsigma(w')=3$. Then Proposition \ref{propTauk} leads to $\dim_{3}(T)=\vert{\cal D}_3(T)\vert=|\{u_{1},u_{2},u_{3},u_{1}',u_{2}',u_{3}'\}|=6$. 

