The viable route is a native fixed-\(k\) basis search, not the paper’s polynomial “largest \(k\)” characterization. I’m implementing \(k=2\) on dense diameter-two graphs: the generator chooses a hidden landmark set first, then samples the graph so those landmarks form an error-correcting distance-signature code. Trees, paths, cycles, and twin-heavy graphs are excluded because Sections 2–4 give direct formulas for them.
