codex
Implemented a native `TRACK = "A"` planted 2-metric-generator family based on the paper’s definition and Theorem 2.2. Fixed-\(k\) hardness is supported by [Schmitz–Vietz–Wanke, Theorem 2](https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.12018).

Files:

- [gen_1312_6840.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/gen_1312_6840.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Random guesses: 0/200,000.
- Six attacks: 0/8 each.
- Exact baseline exhausted 100,000 nodes.
- Answer: 23 characters, 8 elements.

The result is not yet shippable: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” across Gemini, Terra, Grok, and Claude. Consequently G9 is honestly marked failed and all oracle transcripts are error-only. No `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an infrastructure blocker, not a failure of the family.

After restoring quota, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1312_6840.py
```
