787:\item $\ $There exist two vertices $w,w'\in \mathcal{M}(T)$, $w\ne w'$, such that the shortest path from $u$ to $w$ and the shortest path from $v$ to $w'$ have empty intersection, or
788:\item $\ $for every vertex $w''\in \mathcal{M}(T)$, it follows that either $v$ belongs to every shortest  path from $u$ to $w''$ or $u$ belongs to every shortest  path from $v$ to $w''$.
792:Therefore, $S$ is an $r$-metric generator for $T$ and, by Theorem \ref{theoMuk}, the proof is complete.
