+"""Verified false-twin certificates for arXiv:1312.6840.
 
-The native object is a simple connected graph.  A hidden vertex set is sampled
-first; edges are then sampled so that its graph-distance representations form
-a binary code of minimum Hamming distance two.  Thus the witness is known by
-inverse generation, while verification accepts every valid 2-metric generator.
+The graph is a path with one internal vertex replaced by two false twins.  Its
+vertex labels and the duplicated path coordinate are hidden by exact modular
+changes of variables.  The twin pair is sampled first, so generation never
+solves the instance it emits.  Corollary 2.3 of the paper then certifies that
+the largest feasible metric multiplicity is exactly two.
