+Working backward gives `f=6`. Its public label is `7*6+4 mod 12 = 10`;
+the exceptional canonical index 11 has label `7*11+4 mod 12 = 9`.
+Thus `<answer>[9, 10]</answer>` is the answer.
+`verify(inst, [9, 10])` returns `(True, "ok")`; dropping one entry returns
+`(False, "wrong number of vertices: expected 2, got 1")`. This demo is
+comfortably hand-solvable.
 
