The final local report is stable: G1–G8 pass, and only G9 is false because the oracle has zero completed attempts. I’m doing a last independent small-graph expansion check now—materializing the succinct demo graphs to confirm the accepted pair is uniquely false-twin under the actual adjacency rule, not just under the verifier’s shortcut.
