codex
Implemented the verified Track B generator based on Theorem 2.2 and Corollary 2.3 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6840).

Files:

- [gen_1312_6840.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/gen_1312_6840.py:1)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1312.6840/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Structure-aware guessing probability: \(1/2{,}000{,}001\approx4.9999975\times10^{-7}\).
- Track B reference algorithm: 31,261,542 modular operations, about 0.9 seconds.
- Compact intended route: at most 78 operations.
- Independent explicit expansion confirmed unique false-twin certificates on 40/40 small instances.
- G9 and overall completion remain blocked: every OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” leaving zero scored oracle attempts.

No `REJECTED.md` was created because the family itself has not failed; external oracle validation is unavailable.
