 ## Caveats
 
-- NP-completeness is worst-case and does not prove the planted distribution
-  hard. Until the required multi-vendor loop completes, the family must not ship.
-- The observed 0/200,000 rate is for a uniform sorted 8-subset. It does not prove
-  zero density or model guided search; a zero-hit 95% upper bound is about
-  `1.5e-5`.
-- The exact attack is capped. It proves only that this implementation explored
-  100,000 nodes without success, not that an unrestricted ILP, SAT encoding, or
-  commercial solver would take long. Those stronger solvers were not run.
-- The spectral panel uses centered-adjacency power iteration, not an SDP or
-  higher-order tensor method. A construction-aware algebraic attack may exist.
-- Canonicalization is exact only because generation rejects graphs whose 1-WL
-  refinement is not discrete. That conditioning is label-invariant but slightly
-  changes the random graph distribution.
+- This is intentionally not a Track A claim. Corollary 2.3 and a linear
+  collision scan make the family easy with ordinary code; the intended
+  difficulty is recognizing and executing the short inverse chain without a
+  tool.
+- G4 conditions on the public image of canonical index `n-1`, because the
+  statement makes that member of the pair free to infer. Its probability is
+  only for a uniform guess of the remaining partner; it says nothing about a
+  solver that reverses some or all updates.
+- The compact-operation count treats each exact subtraction, reduction, sign
+  change, parity correction, division, multiplication, or addition as one
+  operation. Large-integer transcription risk remains even below the cap.
+- The graph is represented succinctly by a complete adjacency rule rather than
+  by two million explicit adjacency rows. This preserves the paper's native
+  graph object but makes representation-aware algebraic attacks relevant.
+- The panel did not try symbolic composition of all affine rounds into one map;
+  that is another successful compact method, not a failing attack, and belongs
+  to the intended Track B solution class.
+- Until the bare and hinted multi-vendor runs produce real attempts, this bundle
+  must not be submitted as hardened.
