One further correction improves G4 honestly: the old statement revealed one member of the pair for free, forcing a marginal \(1/n\) guessing probability. I’m hiding both canonical preimages with two bijective coordinate chains—one prime-field power chain and one affine chain—while keeping the graph exactly a relabelled one-vertex blow-up of a path. The structure-aware candidate language is then all unordered vertex pairs, not an artificially favorable prior.
apply patch
