The family inverse-generates a succinctly represented path with one duplicated internal coordinate. The answer is its unique false-twin pair, certified using Theorem 2.2 and Corollary 2.3 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6840).

Local results:

- All local gates pass.
- G4: 0/200,000 guesses; exact density \(1/500{,}002{,}500{,}003\).
- Reference algorithm: 911,574 coordinates and 28,306,454 modular operations.
- Six attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Answer: 2 atoms; compact route: 152 operations.
- Independent explicit-graph audit: 20/20 passed.

No `REJECTED.md` was created because hardness was blocked by quota, not disproved. Restore OpenRouter quota and rerun the three harness arms to determine the final shipping verdict.
